      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The concept of algorithms \"sensing a vibration\" or energy is not a recognized technical feature of current social media design. These systems rely on measurable data points like engagement time, interactions, and content patterns, not subjective emotional states. While algorithms certainly reinforce group norms by prioritizing \"liked\" or popular content, the idea of them isolating you based on an invisible personal energy field is more akin to social theory than digital mechanics. Focus on how strong in your *actions* and content are, as that is what the system can actually process.",
